unit3_text:
Module III: Insurance and Risk Management (8 Hours) 
Role of Insurance in Managing Risk; Meaning, Nature and Importance of Insurance; Purpose and Functions of 
Insurance; Classification of Insurance; Life Insurance and General Insurance; Insurance Production Process; 
Relationship between Insurance and Risk; Insurance and Economic Development; Insurance as a Social Security Tool; 
Determinants of Insurance Market Structure; Insurance Distribution Channels; Reinsurance: Meaning, Purpose, 
Importance and Forms of Reinsurance.

unit5_text:
Module V: Regulatory Compliance and Emerging Trends in Insurance Risk Management (8 Hours) 
Regulatory Framework of Insurance Industry; Role of Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDAI); 
Regulatory Compliance Requirements for Insurance Companies; Corporate Governance in Insurance Sector; Risk 
Management Practices in Insurance Organizations; Emerging Trends and Challenges in Insurance Risk Management; 
InsurTech and Digital Insurance; Artificial Intelligence in Insurance Risk Assessment; Data Analytics in Insurance; Ethical 
Considerations and Social Responsibility in Insurance Industry.
